cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: Sleight
abstract: "Sleight is an s-expression language pairing Kernel-style dynamism with static types: restricted dependent types, erased/many/unique multiplicities, termination checking, memory location tracking, and LLMs as intended authors. This repository holds its specification, a reference interpreter in OCaml, a self-hosted compiler to OCaml written in Sleight, and a Lean 4 interpreter for a minimal fragment with a machine-checked proof that well-typed programs evaluate to a value of their type."
authors:
  - family-names: Marion
    given-names: Eric Michael
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-8519-6942"
repository-code: "https://github.com/emmarion/sleight"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - programming languages
  - dependent types
  - type theory
  - multiplicities
  - proof erasure
  - termination checking
  - certified programming
  - in-place update
  - OCaml
  - type-in-type
  - macros
  - Kernel
  - self-hosting compiler
  - Lean 4
  - LLM-assisted programming
  - s-expressions
  - memory location tracking
